  "question": {
    "text": "In a certain town,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the families own a phone and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;own a car;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>%</mo></math> families own neither a phone nor a car and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn></math> families own both a car and a phone. Consider the following three statements:<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> families own both a car and a phone.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>%</mo></math> families own either a car or a phone.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40000</mn></math> families live in the town.<br /><br />Then,"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Only&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;are correct",
