  "solution": {
    "text": "Let set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;contains families which own a phone and set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> contain families which own a car.<br /><br />If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>65</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;families own neither a phone nor a car, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;will own either a phone or a car<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mi>%</mi></math><br /><br />Also we know that<br /><br /><math><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>%</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;families own both phone and car and it is given to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn></math> .<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>%</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40000</mn></math><br /><br />Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are correct."
  }
